concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-economic-disruption-act-2021-sch-1-sec-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 Subsection 400.1(1) of the Criminal Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "Insert: proceeds of general crime means any money or other property that is wholly or partly derived or realised, directly or indirectly, by any person from the commission of: (a) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or (b) a foreign offence. proceeds of indictable crime means: (a) any money or other property that is wholly or partly derived or realised, directly or indirectly, by any person from the commission of a particular offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign country that may be dealt with as an indictable offence (even if it may, in some circumstances, be dealt with as a summary offence); or (b) any money or other property that is wholly or partly derived or realised, directly or indirectly, by any person from the commission of an offence of a particular kind against a law of the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign  Schedule 1  Money laundering" ;
    skos:definition "Insert: proceeds of general crime means any money or other property that is wholly or partly derived or realised, directly or indirectly, by any person from the commission of: (a) an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; or (b) a foreign offence. proceeds of indictable crime means: (a) any money or other property that is wholly or partly derived or realised, directly or indirectly, by any person from the commission of a particular offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign country that may be dealt with as an indictable offence (even if it may, in some circumstances, be dealt with as a summary offence); or (b) any money or other property that is wholly or partly derived or realised, directly or indirectly, by any person from the commission of an offence of a particular kind against a law of the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign  Schedule 1  Money laundering"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "1b2da816e82ae750e035007b7c7e0867be4c202f85dd71c4b7e08860d08be3fb" ;
    cof:pageNumber "9"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Defines 'proceeds of general crime' and 'proceeds of indictable crime'" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
