    skos:definition "(2) For the purposes of this Division, if: (a) a person (the first person) engages in conduct; and (b) the first person’s conduct causes another person to deal with money or other property (within the meaning of subsection (1)); and (c) the first person is reckless as to whether the first person’s conduct causes the other person to deal with the money or property; the first person is taken to have dealt with the money or property."@en ;
