    values:originalText "(1A) A person commits an offence if:  Money laundering  Schedule 1 General amendments  Part 1 No. 3, 2021 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Economic Disruption) Act 2021 (a) the person engages in conduct in relation to money or other property; and (b) the money or property is, and the person believes it to be, proceeds of general crime; and (c) the conduct concealed or disguised any or all of the following: (i) the nature of the money or property; (ii) the value of the money or property; (iii) the source of the money or property; (iv) the location of the money or property; (v) any disposition of the money or property; (vi) any movement of the money or property; (vii) any rights in respect of the money or property; (viii) the identity of any person who has rights in respect of the money or property; (ix) the identity of any person who has effective control of the money or property; and (d) when the conduct occurs, the value of the money and other property is $100,000 or more. Penalty: Imprisonment for 20 years, or 1200 penalty units, or both." ;
