    skos:prefLabel "27(1B) After subsection 400.4(1) of the Criminal Code"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-27-ss-1b ;
    values:originalText "(1B) A person commits an offence if: (a) on 2 or more occasions, the person engages in conduct in relation to money or other property; and (b) for each occasion, the money or property is, and the person believes it to be, proceeds of general crime; and (c) for each occasion, the conduct concealed or disguised any or all of the following: (i) the nature of the money or property; (ii) the value of the money or property; (iii) the source of the money or property; (iv) the location of the money or property; (v) any disposition of the money or property; (vi) any movement of the money or property; (vii) any rights in respect of the money or property;  Schedule 1  Money laundering" ;
