doc:sch-3-sec-14 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "14 Transitional—section 57 of the Proceeds of Crime Act" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Despite the amendment made by item 1, the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 continues to apply, in relation to: (a) an application made before the commencement of this item for an order under section 57 of that Act; and (b) an order made under section 57 of that Act: (i) after the commencement of this item, in response to such an application; or (ii) before the commencement of this item; as if that amendment had not been made." ;
    cof:pageNumber "50"^^xsd:integer .

concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-economic-disruption-act-2021-sch-3-sec-15 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "15 Transitional—sections 103 and 104 of the Proceeds of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-15 ;
    values:originalText "Crime Act 2002 Despite the amendments made by items 2 to 5, the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 continues to apply, in relation to: (a) an application made before the commencement of this item for an order under section 103 of that Act; and (b) an order made under section 103 of that Act: (i) after the commencement of this item, in response to such an application; or (ii) before the commencement of this item; as if those amendments had not been made.  Benefit  Schedule 4 Amendments  Part 1 No. 3, 2021 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Economic Disruption) Act 2021" ;
    skos:definition "Crime Act 2002 Despite the amendments made by items 2 to 5, the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 continues to apply, in relation to: (a) an application made before the commencement of this item for an order under section 103 of that Act; and (b) an order made under section 103 of that Act: (i) after the commencement of this item, in response to such an application; or (ii) before the commencement of this item; as if those amendments had not been made.  Benefit  Schedule 4 Amendments  Part 1 No. 3, 2021 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Economic Disruption) Act 2021"@en ;
