concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-economic-disruption-act-2021-sch-7-sec-31 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "31 At the end of section 275"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-7-sec-31 ;
    values:originalText "Add: (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is required by a notice under paragraph 270(1)(c) to give evidence by video link; and (b) the person refuses or fails: (i) to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or (ii) to answer a question that the person is required to answer by the *Official Trustee or a person authorised under that paragraph, as the case may be. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months or 30 penalty units, or both. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is required by a notice under paragraph 270(1)(d) to give evidence by telephone; and (b) the person refuses or fails:  Official Trustee  Schedule 7 General amendments  Part 1 No. 3, 2021 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Economic Disruption) Act 2021 (i) to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or (ii) to answer a question that the person is required to answer by the *Official Trustee or a person authorised under that paragraph, as the case may be. Penalty for contravention of this subsection:Imprisonment for 6 months or 30 penalty units, or both." ;
    skos:definition "Add: (2) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is required by a notice under paragraph 270(1)(c) to give evidence by video link; and (b) the person refuses or fails: (i) to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or (ii) to answer a question that the person is required to answer by the *Official Trustee or a person authorised under that paragraph, as the case may be. Penalty: Imprisonment for 6 months or 30 penalty units, or both. (3) A person commits an offence if: (a) the person is required by a notice under paragraph 270(1)(d) to give evidence by telephone; and (b) the person refuses or fails:  Official Trustee  Schedule 7 General amendments  Part 1 No. 3, 2021 Crimes Legislation Amendment (Economic Disruption) Act 2021 (i) to be sworn or to make an affirmation; or (ii) to answer a question that the person is required to answer by the *Official Trustee or a person authorised under that paragraph, as the case may be. Penalty for contravention of this subsection:Imprisonment for 6 months or 30 penalty units, or both."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f552a1e79bdc74d313b3f0f000e309faa363c9b81f8db6b9d0fb2b41f0dcea48" ;
    cof:pageNumber "74"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-economic-disruption-act-2021-sch-7-sec-31-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-economic-disruption-act-2021-sch-7-sec-31-ss-3 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
