    prov:wasDerivedFrom <crimes-legislation-amendment-economic-disruption-act-2021.pdf> ;
    dc:source "crimes-legislation-amendment-economic-disruption-act-2021.pdf, p.81" .
doc:sch-7-sec-298e a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "298E Channelling State/Territory grants through the COAG" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Reform Fund (1) If the Minister decides that a grant of financial assistance should be made to a State or Territory under section 298A, the Minister must, by writing, direct that, as soon as practicable, a specified amount (which must equal the amount of the grant) is to be: (a) debited from the *Confiscated Assets Account; and (b) credited to the *COAG Reform Fund. (2) The direction must be expressed to be given in order to enable the amount to be debited from the *COAG Reform Fund for the purpose of making the grant. (3) Two or more directions under subsection (1) may be set out in the same document.  Schedule 7  Official Trustee" ;
    cof:pageNumber "81"^^xsd:integer .

